    stem: "A nurse auscultates the precordium of a 48-year-old client presenting with dyspnea on exertion. The nurse identifies a harsh, blowing holosystolic murmur heard loudest at the fifth left intercostal space at the midclavicular line (apex), radiating into the left axilla. Which valvular defect is responsible for this murmur?",
