    stem: "A client who underwent percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) via the right femoral artery with drug-eluting stent placement 2 hours ago complains of sudden, worsening severe right flank and lower back pain accompanied by lightheadedness. Blood pressure drops from 128/76 to 84/50 mmHg, pulse accelerates to 118 beats/min, and the puncture site dressing is dry with no external hematoma. Which complication should the nurse suspect?",
