    rationale: "Standard patient teaching for sublingual nitroglycerin: dissolve under tongue (do not swallow); take 1 tablet at chest pain onset. If pain persists or worsens after 5 minutes, call emergency services (EMS) immediately and take a second tablet (maximum 3 tablets in 15 minutes). Nitroglycerin is strictly contraindicated within 24-48 hours of phosphodiesterase-5 inhibitors (sildenafil, tadalafil) due to catastrophic refractory hypotension. Tablets must be stored in original dark amber glass bottles. Why the other options fail: Swallowing the tablet defeats sublingual absorption; sildenafil with a nitrate can cause catastrophic hypotension and is contraindicated within twenty-four to forty-eight hours; heat and light degrade the tablets. The correct teaching is one tablet at once, repeat after five minutes, call emergency services if it persists.",
