    correctChoiceId: "b",
    rationale: "The rhythm is pulseless Ventricular Fibrillation (V-Fib), a lethal shockable cardiac arrest rhythm characterized by quivering ventricles producing zero cardiac output. The immediate ACLS algorithm requires: 1) Call code/help, 2) Start high-quality CPR (chest compressions), and 3) Deliver immediate unsynchronized defibrillation as soon as the manual defibrillator/AED arrives. Synchronized cardioversion is contraindicated because there are no QRS complexes to track. Why the other options fail: Synchronised cardioversion is for a rhythm with a pulse and cannot be synchronised to a chaotic baseline; atropine is for symptomatic bradycardia and does nothing in cardiac arrest from ventricular fibrillation; a fluid bolus does not restart a fibrillating heart. Compressions and immediate defibrillation are what save the client.",
