    categorySlug: "med-surg",
    stem: "A 29-year-old presents to the emergency department reporting sharp, retrosternal chest pain that worsens significantly with deep inspiration, coughing, and lying flat on his back. The pain is noticeably relieved when he sits upright and leans forward. Auscultation reveals a scratchy, high-pitched grating sound at the lower left sternal border. Which condition is most consistent with these clinical findings?",
