    rationale: "Clients with high-risk cardiac conditions (prosthetic heart valves, prosthetic repair material, prior history of infective endocarditis, or unrepaired cyanotic congenital heart disease) require prophylactic antibiotic coverage (typically oral amoxicillin 2 g 30-60 minutes prior) before dental procedures involving gingival manipulation to prevent bacteremia from establishing infective endocarditis on the prosthetic valve. Why the other options fail: The antibiotic is not aimed at the dental surgical site, is not given because of the anticoagulant, and does not dissolve toxins or treat rheumatic fever. It covers the transient bacteraemia that would otherwise seed a prosthetic valve and cause endocarditis.",
