    stem: "A client admitted 2 days ago with an acute left femoral deep vein thrombosis (DVT) on therapeutic enoxaparin suddenly rings the call bell complaining of sharp left-sided pleuritic chest pain, dyspnea, and impending doom. Pulse is 116 bpm, respiratory rate is 28 breaths/min, and oxygen saturation has dropped from 98% to 88% on room air. What should the nurse do FIRST?",
