    categorySlug: "pharmacology-parenteral",
    stem: "A 70-year-old client with heart failure taking oral digoxin 0.25 mg daily presents with fatigue, loss of appetite, nausea, and complains of \"yellowish-green halos around room lights.\" The nurse checks the apical pulse for 60 seconds and counts 48 beats/min. Serum potassium is 3.1 mEq/L. Which clinical action must the nurse take first?",
